# Force LF line endings for all text/source/data files, regardless of the
# checkout platform's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows clone
# with the common core.autocrlf=true converts every text file to CRLF on
# checkout, which changes its bytes -- and therefore its SHA-256 hash. That
# silently broke `npm run verify` (scripts/hash_sources.js) on a normal
# Windows checkout even though the exact same commit passed on Linux/macOS
# or a byte-preserving Windows clone. Confirmed 2026-07-13.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts: never line-ending-convert or diff these. SQLite DBs are
# the mushaf-layout databases under data/raw and data/layouts; the rest are
# images and a spreadsheet under docs/ and assets/.
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
